# Git LFS carries the example captures under examples/.
#
# They are demo files first — small, curated, and openable by hand — but
# they are still binaries, and a binary committed raw stays in every clone
# forever. LFS keeps the pointer in history and the bytes out of it.
#
# The scope is deliberately examples/ and no wider. The MDF fixtures under
# crates/cannet-mdf/tests/fixtures/ are read by `cargo test --workspace`,
# so putting them behind LFS would make the default test suite fail in a
# clone that has not fetched the objects; the Tauri icons have to be real
# bytes at build time. Those stay in plain git.
#
# A clone needs `git lfs install` once and `git lfs pull` to turn these
# pointers back into files — see README § Prerequisites. Several Rust
# tests read examples/ captures, so a clone without them fails the suite.
examples/**/*.blf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
examples/**/*.mf4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
